],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"source":["plt.figure(figsize=(15, 6))\n","\n","palette = sns.color_palette(\"mako\", len(effective_and_variable))\n","\n","ax= sns.barplot(\n","    data = effective_and_variable.reset_index(),\n","    x = \"DRUG\",\n","    y = \"median\",\n","    hue = \"median\",\n","    palette = palette,\n","    legend = False\n",")\n","\n","plt.title(\"Top most effective and high variable drugs\", fontsize = 14)\n","plt.xlabel(\"Drug Name\", fontsize = 12)\n","plt.ylabel(\"Median IC50\", fontsize = 12)\n","plt.xticks(rotation = 45)\n","\n","ax.errorbar(\n","    x = np.arange(len(effective_and_variable)),\n","    y = effective_and_variable[\"median\"],\n","    yerr = effective_and_variable[\"std\"],\n","    fmt = \"o\",\n","    color = \"grey\",\n","    capsize = 2\n",")\n","\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["To analyze drug effectiveness and identify patterns in drug sensitivity, LN_IC50 values were examined across drugs and cancer cell lines. Drug effectiveness was interpreted based on LN_IC50, where lower values indicate higher sensitivity and higher values indicate resistance.\n","\n","The analysis focused on:\n","\n","Most effective drugs: Drugs with consistently low LN_IC50 values across cell lines, indicating strong sensitivity.\n","Least effective drugs: Drugs with higher LN_IC50 values, suggesting reduced sensitivity or resistance.\n","Highly variable drugs: Drugs showing large variation in LN_IC50 across cancer types, indicating context-dependent responses."],"metadata":{"id":"zNs_WYqchsQo"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Most effective drugs (lowest median IC50)\n","most_effective = (\n","    gdsc.groupby(\"DRUG\")[\"IC50\"]\n","    .median()\n","    .sort_values()\n","    .head(5)\n","    .index\n",")\n","\n","# Least effective drugs (highest median IC50)\n","least_effective = (\n","    gdsc.groupby(\"DRUG\")[\"IC50\"]\n","    .median()\n","    .sort_values(ascending=False)\n","    .head(5)\n","    .index\n",")\n","\n","# Subset data\n","plot_data = gdsc[\n","    gdsc[\"DRUG\"].isin(list(most_effective) + list(least_effective))\n","]\n","\n","# Create category column\n","plot_data[\"Category\"] = plot_data[\"DRUG\"].apply(\n","    lambda x: \"Most Effective\" if x in most_effective else \"Least Effective\"\n",")\n","\n","# Plot\n","plt.figure(figsize=(14, 6))\n","\n","sns.boxplot(\n","    data=plot_data,\n","    x=\"DRUG\",\n","    y=\"IC50\",\n","    hue=\"Category\"\n",")\n","\n","plt.title(\"Most vs Least Effective Drugs\")\n","plt.xlabel(\"Drug\")\n","plt.ylabel(\"IC50\")\n","plt.xticks(rotation=45)\n","\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"id":"O3wKCp3fir9N","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1789215925433,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":530,"user":{"displayName":"Himabindu Kumdam","userId":"05411869555977081730"}},"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":714},"outputId":"f9a017f7-46ca-44ba-af62-b8264e6eb709"},"execution_count":31,"outputs":[{"output_type":"stream","name":"stderr","text":["/tmp/ipykernel_2921/553326449.py:25: SettingWithCopyWarning: \n","A value is trying to be set on a copy of a slice from a DataFrame.\n","Try using .loc[row_indexer,col_indexer] = value instead\n","\n","See the caveats in the documentation: https://pandas.pydata.org/pandas-docs/stable/user_guide/indexing.html#returning-a-view-versus-a-copy\n","  plot_data[\"Category\"] = plot_data[\"DRUG\"].apply(\n"]},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1400x600 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The boxplots compare IC50 distributions for the most and least effective drugs. Most effective drugs show consistently lower IC50 values, indicating stronger sensitivity across cancer cell lines, whereas least effective drugs display higher IC50 values and reduced potency. The spread of the distributions also highlights variability in drug response between cell lines."],"metadata":{"id":"OJ2-6C7NB4oS"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":[],"metadata":{"id":"okmM78pvB4AP"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## 7. Cancer Type-Drug Sensitivity Analysis\n","###EXPLORING HOW DIFFERENT CELL LINES RESPOND TO DRUGS\n"," In this section, we transition our report from globally evaluating drug compounds to examining how different tumor lineages (cancer types) respond to these therapies. We stratify drug sensitivity by lineage to determine:\n","1. **Lineage-Specific Vulnerabilities:** Which distinct cancer types are natively sensitive or inherently resistant across specific drug classes.\n","2. **Mechanistic Intersections:** How targeted molecular pathways interact with specific cancer origins to drive therapeutic responses.\n","\n","---\n","\n","### Subsection 7.1: Hierarchical Clustering of Lineage-Drug Intersections\n","To find shared biology across distinct anatomical solid tumors, we construct a pivot matrix of mean drug sensitivity ($LN\\_IC50$) across cancer lineages and apply a dual-metric hierarchical clustermap.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"PKrxEDzTr-I-"}},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":34,"metadata":{"id":"MvoBZnBMr-I_","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1789216104898,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":16,"user":{"displayName":"Himabindu Kumdam","userId":"05411869555977081730"}}},"outputs":[],"source":["subset_drugs = gdsc[gdsc[\"DRUG\"].isin(effective_and_variable.index)]"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":35,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":1000},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1789216106788,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":678,"user":{"displayName":"Himabindu Kumdam","userId":"05411869555977081730"}},"outputId":"4a95860b-09aa-491f-afc7-9edc26afc7c8","id":"x2TCob4hr-I_"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1200x1000 with 4 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"source":["import seaborn as sns\n","import matplotlib.pyp