{\n      \"column\": \"TARGET_PATHWAY\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"dtype\": \"category\",\n        \"num_unique_values\": 7,\n        \"samples\": [\n          \"DNA replication\",\n          \"Mitosis\"\n        ],\n        \"semantic_type\": \"\",\n        \"description\": \"\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}"}},"metadata":{},"execution_count":83}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Relative Selectivity Profiles (Z-Score)\n","Next, we normalize the matrix around Z-scores to strip away absolute baseline differences. This explicitly isolates lineage-specific hypersensitivity (blue) and targeted resistance nodes (red).\n"],"metadata":{"id":"tAsiOAPMmRZe"}},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":36,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":1000},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1789216161663,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":672,"user":{"displayName":"Himabindu Kumdam","userId":"05411869555977081730"}},"outputId":"2fa2a125-edb8-41f0-c10b-56c0087ea29d","id":"CfHWqpg_JN0m"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1200x1000 with 4 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"source":["import seaborn as sns\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","\n","# Pivot: Cancer × Drug\n","cancer_drug_matrix = subset_drugs.pivot_table(\n","    index=\"CANCER_TYPE\",\n","    columns=\"DRUG\",\n","    values=\"Z_SCORE\",\n","    aggfunc=\"mean\"\n",")\n","\n","# Optional: drop cancers with too many missing values\n","#cancer_drug_matrix = cancer_drug_matrix.dropna(thresh=5)\n","\n","cancer_drug_matrix = cancer_drug_matrix.fillna(cancer_drug_matrix.mean())\n","\n","# Clustermap\n","g = sns.clustermap(\n","    cancer_drug_matrix,\n","    cmap=\"RdBu\",\n","    center=0,\n","    figsize=(12, 10),\n","    linewidths=0.5,\n","    metric=\"euclidean\",\n","    method=\"average\"\n",")\n","\n","plt.title(\"Cancer Type vs Mean Z score\", pad=100)\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### 🔬 Key Discoveries from the Z-Score Clustermap\n","\n","* **Lineage Bi-Segregation:** Hierarchical clustering cleanly partitions the dataset into two structural response phenotypes: a globally hypersensitive hematological block (`CLL`, `ALL`, `DLBC`, `LAML`) and a highly resistant solid tumor block (`PAAD`, `SKCM`, `COAD/READ`).\n","* **Mechanistic Selectivity:** The Z-score normalization uncovers explicit biomarker signatures. For instance, while solid tumors display broad-spectrum resistance, isolated sensitivity nodes—such as the pronounced vulnerability of Uterine (`UCEC`) and Breast (`BRCA`) cohorts to specific DNA-replicative agents (*Mitoxantrone*, *Gemcitabine*)—become visually apparent.\n","* **Target Co-Clustering:** Chemotherapeutics targeting shared downstream pathways (e.g., *Paclitaxel*, *Docetaxel*, and *Vinblastine* targeting mitosis) cluster tightly together along the horizontal axis, validating that functional pathway determinants dictate the relative selectivity profiles.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"WVNMVfrxmnMw"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":[],"metadata":{"id":"ewcp4ayio8HQ"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Select top effective and variable drugs\n","selected_drugs = effective_and_variable.index\n","\n","# Subset dataset\n","subset_drugs = gdsc[gdsc[\"DRUG\"].isin(selected_drugs)]\n","\n","# Create cancer type × drug matrix\n","heatmap_data = subset_drugs.pivot_table(\n","    index=\"CANCER_TYPE\",\n","    columns=\"DRUG\",\n","    values=\"IC50\",\n","    aggfunc=\"median\"\n",")\n","\n","# Plot heatmap\n","plt.figure(figsize=(14, 10))\n","\n","sns.heatmap(\n","    heatmap_data,\n","    cmap=\"RdBu_r\",\n","    center=heatmap_data.median().median()\n",")\n","\n","plt.title(\"Drug × Cancer Type Sensitivity Heatmap\")\n","plt.xlabel(\"Drug\")\n","plt.ylabel(\"Cancer Type\")\n","\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":1000},"id":"8JXXtb-lCgxd","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1779073424703,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":619,"user":{"displayName":"Himabindu Kumdam","userId":"05411869555977081730"}},"outputId":"11271b01-30f5-4412-e97f-1a9119fca6d7"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1400x1000 with 2 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## Lineage Sensitivity Ranking Insights\n","\n","* **The Hematological Boundary:** The absolute top tier of drug vulnerability is exclusively dominated by liquid and hematological malignancies. Chronic Lymphocytic Leukemia (`CLL`), Acute Myeloid Leukemia (`LAML`), Acute Lymphoblastic Leukemia (`ALL`), and Diffuse Large B-Cell Lymphoma (`DLBC`) display the absolute lowest global median $LN\\_IC50$ ranges.\n","* **Solid Tumor Obstinacy:** Conversely, epithelial-derived solid tumors anchor the bottom tier of the rankings. Pancreatic Adenocarcinoma (`PAAD`), Mesothelioma (`MESO`), Uterine Corpus Endometrial Carcinoma (`UCEC`), and Liver Hepatocellular Carcinoma (`LIHC`) display high shifts toward baseline resistance.\n","* **The Variance Story (IQR Bars):** Look closely at the error bars (IQR). Solid tumors like Breast Cancer (`BRCA`) and Lung Adenocarcinoma (`LUAD`) display significantly wider error bands compared to the tightly constrained liquid malignancies. This confirms that these solid cohorts possess massive sub-clonal heterogeneity, meaning their therapeutic response varies drastically from patient to patient, necessitating personalized targeted regimens.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"A4bF2Jdcn5jW"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["import numpy as np\n","import seaborn as sns\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","\n","# Group by cancer type → compute stats\n","summary = (\n","    gdsc.groupby(\"CANCER_TYPE\")[\"IC50\"]\n","    .agg(\n","        median=\"median\",\n","        q1=lambda x: np.percentile(x, 25),\n","        q3=lambda x: np.percentile(x, 75),\n","        n=\"count\"\n","    )\n","    .reset_index()\n",")\n","\n","# Compute IQR error bars\n","summary[\"lower\"] = summary[\"median\"] - summary[\"q1\"]\n","summary[\"upper\"] = summary[\"q3\"] - summary[\"median\"]\n","\n","# Sort (most sensitive at top)\n","summary = summary.sort_values(\"median\", ascending=True)\n","\n","# Plot\n","plt.figure(figsize=(10, 12))\n","\n","ax = sns.barplot(\n","    data=summary,\n","    x=\"median\",\n","    y=\"CANCER_TYPE\",\n","    hue=\"CANCER_TYPE\",\n","    palette=\"coolwarm\"\n",")\n","\n","# Add error bars manually\n","plt.errorbar(\n","    summary[\"median\"],\n","    range(len(summary)),  # positions on y-axis\n","    xerr=[summary[\"lower\"], summary[\"upper\"]],\n","    fmt=\"none\",\n","    ecolor=\"black\",\n","    capsize=3\n",")\n","\n","# Labels\n","plt.xlabel(\"Median LN_IC50 (lower = more sensitive)\")\n","plt.ylabel(\"Cancer Type\")\n","plt.title(\"Cancer Type Sensitivity Ranking (with IQR)\")\n","\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":1000},"id":"hmUv1k_E0oCi","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1789216633683,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":588,"user":{"displayName":"Himabindu Kumdam","userId":"05411869555977081730"}},"outputId":"139ec585-08ad-4bec-e891-788ea19cccae"},"execution_count":38,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x1200 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["drug sensitivity was compared across cancer types using median values with interquartile range (IQR) as shown in the figure. This analysis enabled identification of the most drug-sensitive cell types as well as those exhibiting selective drug responses.\n","\n","*  Most drug-sensitive cell types:\n","Hematological cancers such as CLL, LAML, ALL, and DLBC showed the lowest median LN_IC50 values, indicating consistently high sensitivity across a wide range of drugs.\n","\n","*  Least sensitive (more resistant) cell types:\n","Solid tumors such as PAAD, MESO, UCEC, and LIHC exhibited higher median LN_IC50 values, indicating reduced overall sensitivity and relative resistance.\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"aGqDMtcmjkBQ"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### 🔬 Phenotypic Landscape and Outlier Dynamics\n","\n","* **Consistent Sensitivity vs. Volatile Resistance:** The highly sensitive hematological cancers (`CLL`, `ALL`, `LAML`) feature tightly compressed boxes, demonstrating that their sensitivity is a uniform feature across almost all cell lines and drug screens. In contrast, resistant solid tumors (`PAAD`, `LIHC`) display expansive horizontal spreads, indicating a highly volatile landscape where a subset of cell lines within the same tumor class defy the resistant average.\n","* **The Long Right Tail (Vulnerability Outliers):** Crucially, almost all the resistant solid tumors at the bottom of the plot exhibit extensive left-ward and right-ward whiskers, alongside numerous individual outlier points. The points stretching into negative territory are of profound clinical interest: they represent specific cell lines that remain highly vulnerable to select drugs despite belonging to an otherwise highly resistant cancer lineage.\n","* **Justification for Statistical Frameworks:** The presence of significant skewness and extensive outliers across these distributions further reinforces why the median—rather than the mean—must be utilized as the central anchor for downstream comparative modeling.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"FjFKg9hLoZkD"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Median IC50 per cancer type\n","\n","# Plot\n","plt.figure(figsize=(12, 8))\n","\n","sns.boxplot(\n","    data=gdsc,\n","    y=\"CANCER_TYPE\",\n","    x=\"IC50\",\n","    order=summary[\"CANCER_TYPE\"],\n","    hue=\"CANCER_TYPE\",\n","    palette=\"coolwarm\"\n",")\n","\n","plt.title(\"Cancer Type Sensitivity Distribution\")\n","plt.xlabel(\"IC50\")\n","plt.ylabel(\"Cancer Type\")\n","\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":807},"id":"YlnbRYVDCZne","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1789216762619,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":1377,"user":{"displayName":"Himabindu Kumdam","userId":"05411869555977081730"}},"outputId":"adf562df-b6c6-4a0e-a763-7f2e294029c2"},"execution_count":40,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1200x800 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### 🔬 Lineage Selectivity and Targeted Potential\n","\n","* **True Lineage Selectivity Defined:** The drugs isolated in this plot exhibit wide vertical box distributions. This high variance across cancer midpoints proves these agents are not globally toxic or globally inert; rather, their structural design interacts uniquely with lineage-specific biology.\n","* **Clinical Biomarker Candidates:** A broad vertical spread on this chart indicates that the compound works exceptionally well against certain cancer types while remaining ineffective against others. These six drugs represent ideal candidates for lineage-specific biomarker discovery, as their efficacy depends heavily on the anatomical site or tissue origin of the tumor.\n","* **Transition to Molecular Mechanism:** Having confirmed that drug sensitivity varies significantly both across and within specific cancer lineages, the next analytical phase must shift from *phenotypic* classifications (tissue types) to *mechanistic* drivers—examining the exact target pathways and genetic changes that dictate these variations.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"RqB2kfUepWIX"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Calculate variability of each drug across cancer types\n","cancer_selectivity = (\n","    gdsc.groupby([\"DRUG\", \"CANCER_TYPE\"])[\"IC50\"]\n","    .median()\n","    .reset_index()\n",")\n","\n","# Standard deviation across cancer types\n","drug_selectivity = (\n","    cancer_selectivity.groupby(\"DRUG\")[\"IC50\"]\n","    .std()\n","    .sort_valu