execution_count":69}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"dn0CdZWPRjyD"},"source":["#  **8. Pathway-level analysis:**\n","\n","*   Identify which target pathways are most sensitive and highly variable based on LN_IC50 values.\n","\n","*  Lower median LN_IC50 indicates higher sensitivity, while higher standard deviation (std) indicates greater variability in drug response across cell lines.\n","\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":43,"metadata":{"id":"yg_kldrsRdRp","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1789217230052,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":23,"user":{"displayName":"Himabindu Kumdam","userId":"05411869555977081730"}}},"outputs":[],"source":["# Group data by target pathway to understand drug response at pathway level\n","# Calculate:\n","# - mean LN_IC50 -> average drug sensitivity\n","# - median LN_IC50 -> measure of typical sensitivity\n","# - std -> variability in drug response across cell lines\n","\n","# Sort pathways by median LN_IC50\n","#  lower median = higher sensitivity\n","#  helps rank pathways from most to least sensitive\n","pathway_stats = gdsc.groupby(\"TARGET_PATHWAY\")[\"IC50\"].agg( # (Opemidimeji) Changed \"LN_IC50\" to \"IC50\"\n","    mean=\"mean\",\n","    median=\"median\",\n","    std=\"std\"\n",").sort_values(by=\"median\")\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":44,"metadata":{"id":"HbQ-nL-kSuJi","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1789217233413,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":46,"user":{"displayName":"Himabindu Kumdam","userId":"05411869555977081730"}}},"outputs":[],"source":["low_median = pathway_stats[\"median\"].quantile(0.25)\n","high_std = pathway_stats[\"std\"].quantile(0.75)\n","\n","important_pathways = pathway_stats[\n","    (pathway_stats[\"median\"] <= low_median) &\n","    (pathway_stats[\"std\"] >= high_std)\n","]\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### 🔬 Systems Biology and Pathway Quadrant Analysis\n","\n","* **The Broad-Spectrum Lethality Quadrant (Bottom Left):** Pathways falling into the lower-left quadrant (below the sensitivity threshold with low standard deviations) represent universal dependencies across cancer cell lines. Therapeutics targeting these networks kill cells effectively regardless of tissue lineage, behaving similarly to classic cytotoxic agents.\n","* **The High-Selectivity Biomarker Quadrant (Top Left):** Pathways positioned in the upper-left quadrant combine sharp potency (low median) with immense volatility (high standard deviation). This profile confirms that while the entire cancer cohort is not uniformly vulnerable to these agents, specific genetic subsets display profound hypersensitivity, making these pathways prime targets for companion biomarker development.\n","* **The Signaling Cascade Buffer (Right Quadrants):** Pathways on the right half of the chart (higher median values) demonstrate more widespread resistance profiles. This distribution indicates that targeting individual downstream signaling cascades frequently allows cancer cells to deploy bypass loops or compensatory networks, shifting the global population average toward survival.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"_3gzXDRlqyI9"}},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":46,"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":601},"id":"XUYdFuUbIaHp","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1789217330652,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":412,"user":{"displayName":"Himabindu Kumdam","userId":"05411869555977081730"}},"outputId":"ce071484-662f-45ed-cc7e-e4f4adfccb21"},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 800x600 with 1 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"source":["import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","import seaborn as sns\n","\n","\n","sns.set(style=\"ticks\")\n","\n","plt.figure(figsize=(8,6))\n","\n","# Scatter plot\n","# Each point = one pathway\n","# x-axis = sensitivity (median LN_IC50)\n","# y-axis = variability (std)\n","sns.scatterplot(\n","    data=pathway_stats,\n","    x=\"median\",\n","    y=\"std\",\n","    s=120,\n","    color=\"#1F4E79\",\n","    edgecolor=\"black\",\n","    linewidth=0.8\n",")\n","\n","# Thresholds\n","# 25th percentile → sensitive pathways\n","# 75th percentile → highly variable pathways\n","median_thresh = pathway_stats[\"median\"].quantile(0.25)\n","std_thresh = pathway_stats[\"std\"].quantile(0.75)\n","\n","# Divide plot into 4 quadrants based on thresholds\n","plt.axvline(median_thresh, linestyle=\"--\")\n","plt.axhline(std_thresh, linestyle=\"--\")\n","\n","\n","# Label the pathways\n","for pathway in pathway_stats.index:\n","    plt.text(\n","        pathway_stats.loc[pathway, \"median\"] + 0.05,\n","        pathway_stats.loc[pathway, \"std\"] + 0.05,\n","        pathway,\n","        fontsize=8,\n","        weight=\"bold\"\n","    )\n","\n","# Axis labels\n","plt.xlabel(\"Median LN_IC50 (Sensitivity)\")\n","plt.ylabel(\"Standard Deviation (Variability)\")\n","\n","# Title\n","plt.title(\"Pathway-Level Drug Sensitivity and Variability\")\n","\n","# Remove top/right spines (clean look)\n","#sns.despine()\n","\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["To analyze drug effectiveness in a biological context, drugs were grouped by their target pathways, and patterns in drug sensitivity (IC50) were examined across these pathways.\n","\n","Drugs targeting core proliferative pathways such as mitosis, cell cycle, and DNA replication showed the highest effectiveness, with consistently low IC50 values across cancer types. In contrast, drugs targeting signaling and regulatory pathways (e.g., RTK, PI3K/MAPK, metabolism) exhibited higher IC50 values and greater variability, indicating reduced or context-dependent sensitivity.\n","\n","These patterns suggest that drugs targeting essential cellular processes tend to be broadly effective, while those targeting signaling pathways show more heterogeneous responses depending on cancer type and molecular context."],"metadata":{"id":"RrFrMLCfsHUd"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### 🔬 Co-Clustering Dynamics and Functional Equivalence\n","\n","* **Validation of Direct Mechanism (The Microtubule Block):** The correlation matrix uncovers tight, dark blocks of high positive correlation ($r > 0.8$) among the taxanes (*Paclitaxel*, *Docetaxel*) and vinca alkaloids (*Vinblastine*, *Vinorelbine*). Despite being distinct chemical structures, their absolute grouping proves that downstream tumor response profiles are governed entirely by their shared functional class: disrupting the mitotic spindle assembly.\n","* **Topoisomerase Congruence:** A secondary distinct cluster emerges containing *Camptothecin*, *Topotecan*, and *SN-38*. This grouping mathematically validates the consistency of the screening assay, showing that compounds targeting Topoisomerase I share near-identical cell-line-specific activation and resistance networks.\n","* **Mechanistic Isolation:** Specialized compounds like *Trametinib* (MEK inhibitor) and *Elesclomol* show negligible correlation against the primary cytotoxic blocks. This independent positioning indicates that targeted therapies bypass broad structural cell-killing pathways, relying instead on unique oncogenic mutations or pathway dependencies specific to individual tumor subgroups.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"aXazN5ZErcmK"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":[],"metadata":{"id":"0kvycWu_taAP"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Create matrix\n","zscore_matrix = gdsc.pivot_table(\n","    index=\"CANCER_TYPE\",\n","    columns=\"TARGET_PATHWAY\",\n","    values=\"Z_SCORE\",\n","    aggfunc=\"mean\"\n",")\n","\n","# Plot heatmap\n","plt.figure(figsize=(16, 10))\n","\n","sns.heatmap(\n","    zscore_matrix,\n","    cmap=\"RdBu_r\",\n","    center=0\n",")\n","\n","plt.title(\"Mean Z-Score Heatmap: Cancer Type × Target Pathway\")\n","plt.xlabel(\"Target Pathway\")\n","plt.ylabel(\"Cancer Type\")\n","\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":100