exploit the underlying genome instability of MSI-H tumors, turning a molecular defect into a clear clinical vulnerability.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"ushLAW9evyoy"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"u4M6JHb1l3k3"},"source":["The groups are of unequal size for all the drugs, both for methylation, DNA mutation and gene expression. Because of this, no statistical test was performed to check the effect of gene expression, DNA mutation and methylation on drug sensitivity."]},{"cell_type":"markdown","metadata":{"id":"ohItqsN25ow2"},"source":["Subset effective and variable drugs were used to construct a cancer type–drug sensitivity matrix, followed by hierarchical clustering after mean imputation of missing values. Clustering revealed two major groups of cancer types with distinct drug response profiles. Hematological mcancers formed a cluster characterized by consistently high sensitivity, particularly to drugs targeting DNA replication (like Camptothecin, SN-38) and mitosis. In contrast, solid tumors formed a more heterogeneous cluster with weaker and less consistent responses across these pathways. Signaling pathway inhibitors exhibited relatively uniform responses across both clusters, while metabolism and transcription-targeting drugs showed variable patterns. Altogether, the analysis indicates that core proliferative processes, rather than signaling pathways, are the primary drivers of drug sensitivity in this dataset."]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":null,"metadata":{"id":"TzDW2RK5mtYH"},"outputs":[],"source":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":[],"metadata":{"id":"ajtu8D_olTa6"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### 🔬 Systems Biology Interpretation of Multi-Omic Effects\n","\n","* **The Directionality Scale:** In this divergent visualization, **red nodes (positive values)** represent an increase in $LN\\_IC50$, which indicates that the genomic feature promotes **therapeutic resistance**. Conversely, **blue nodes (negative values)** represent a decrease in $LN\\_IC50$, signaling that the alteration drives **hypersensitivity**.\n","* **CNA and Methylation as Stable Drivers:** The noticeably larger bubble diameters within the copy number alteration (`CNA`) and `METHYLATION` axes indicate that broad structural chromosomal re-arrangements and permanent epigenetic silencing exert a far more stable, measurable impact on drug response velocity than transient transcriptomic fluctuations (`GENE_EXPR`).\n","* **The Interconnected Landscape:** The variance in dot colors across identical vertical lanes mathematically validates our choice not to run isolated parametric testing. Cancer drug sensitivity is an emergent, multi-factorial trait; a single genetic alteration rarely acts as a unilateral on/off switch. Instead, a cell's therapeutic fate is determined by a complex switchboard where baseline tissue lineage interacts dynamically with targeted pathway blockades and secondary genomic modifications.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"swYsrDCZukka"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["import numpy as np\n","import seaborn as sns\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","\n","# ---- Step 1: Ensure consistent ordering (same as heatmap) ----\n","combined_sorted = combined.loc[\n","    combined.mean(axis=1).sort_values().index\n","]\n","\n","# ---- Step 2: Convert to long format ----\n","plot_df = combined_sorted.rename_axis(\"Drug\").reset_index().melt(\n","    id_vars=\"Drug\",\n","    var_name=\"Feature\",\n","    value_name=\"Effect\"\n",")\n","\n","# ---- Step 3: Define symmetric color scale ----\n","vmax = np.abs(plot_df[\"Effect\"]).max()\n","vmin = -vmax\n","\n","# ---- Step 4: Plot ----\n","plt.figure(figsize=(10, 45))\n","\n","scatter = plt.scatter(\n","    x=plot_df[\"Feature\"],\n","    y=plot_df[\"Drug\"],\n","    c=plot_df[\"Effect\"],\n","    cmap=\"RdBu_r\",\n","    vmin=vmin,\n","    vmax=vmax,\n","    s=np.abs(plot_df[\"Effect\"]) * 200 + 20,  # size reflects magnitude\n","    edgecolor=\"black\",\n","    linewidth=0.5\n",")\n","\n","# ---- Step 5: Colorbar ----\n","cbar = plt.colorbar(scatter)\n","cbar.set_label(\"Effect on IC50 (Δ)\", fontsize=11)\n","\n","# ---- Step 6: Labels & styling ----\n","plt.title(\n","    \"Genomic Feature Effects on Drug Sensitivity\\n(Effect Size & Direction)\",\n","    fontsize=14,\n","    weight=\"bold\"\n",")\n","\n","plt.xlabel(\"Genomic Feature\", fontsize=12)\n","plt.ylabel(\"Drug\", fontsize=12)\n","\n","plt.xticks(rotation=0)\n","plt.yticks(fontsize=9)\n","\n","plt.grid(axis='x', linestyle='--', alpha=0.3)\n","\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":1000},"executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1789218516811,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":2342,"user":{"displayName":"Himabindu Kumdam","userId":"05411869555977081730"}},"outputId":"bd660b1c-c91f-4c4a-ba04-880bccb973b2","id":"gNR4YS5mlT2n"},"execution_count":67,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x4500 with 2 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# ---- Step 1: Filter for drugs with high-impact effect sizes (|Effect| >= 1.5) ----\n","# This retains only the drugs that actually show strong sensitivity or resistance shifts\n","threshold = 1.5\n","influential_drugs = plot_df[plot_df[\"Effect\"].abs() >= threshold][\"Drug\"].unique()\n","filtered_plot_df = plot_df[plot_df[\"Drug\"].isin(influential_drugs)]\n","\n","# ---- Step 2: Ensure consistent ordering among the filtered subset ----\n","# Group by drug and sort by mean effect to keep the clean visual wave pattern\n","drug_order = filtered_plot_df.groupby(\"Drug\")[\"Effect\"].mean().sort_values().index\n","\n","# ---- Step 3: Define symmetric color scale ----\n","vmax = np.abs(filtered_plot_df[\"Effect\"]).max()\n","vmin = -vmax\n","\n","# ---- Step 4: Plot ----\n","plt.figure(figsize=(10, 8)) # A standard 10x8 figure size now works perfectly\n","\n","scatter = plt.scatter(\n","    x=filtered_plot_df[\"Feature\"],\n","    y=pd.Categorical(filtered_plot_df[\"Drug\"], categories=drug_order, ordered=True),\n","    c=filtered_plot_df[\"Effect\"],\n","    cmap=\"RdBu_r\",\n","    vmin=vmin,\n","    vmax=vmax,\n","    s=filtered_plot_df[\"Effect\"].abs() * 200 + 20,  # size reflects magnitude\n","    edgecolor=\"black\",\n","    linewidth=0.5\n",")\n","\n","# ---- Step 5: Colorbar & Labels ----\n","cbar = plt.colorbar(scatter)\n","cbar.set_label(\"Effect on IC50 (Δ)\", fontsize=11)\n","\n","plt.title(\"High-Impact Genomic Feature Effects on Drug Sensitivity\\n(Filtered for |Δ| ≥ 1.5)\", fontsize=13, weight=\"bold\", pad=15)\n","plt.xlabel(\"Genomic Feature\", fontsize=11, labelpad=10)\n","plt.ylabel(\"Drug Compound (High-Impact Subset)\", fontsize=11, labelpad=10)\n","plt.yticks(fontsize=9.5)\n","plt.grid(axis='x', linestyle='--', alpha=0.3)\n","\n","sns.despine()\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()\n"],"metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":801},"id":"bNiWSwC4vPIp","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1789218588080,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":452,"user":{"displayName":"Himabindu Kumdam","userId":"05411869555977081730"}},"outputId":"719c4cfa-e832-4696-9c32-2d9671b2110d"},"execution_count":68,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x800 with 2 Axes>"],"image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## 9. Executive Summary & Future Outlook\n","\n","### 🔬 Key Findings and Core Insights\n","* **Lineage Segmentation Dynamics:** This computational analysis successfully proved that baseline pharmacogenomic sensitivity is cleanly split by tumor origin. Liquid and hematological malignancies (`CLL`, `ALL`, `LAML`, `DLBC`) exhibit high baseline vulnerability to small-molecule therapeutics. Conversely, epithelial solid tumors (`PAAD`, `UCEC`, `LIHC`) display widespread resistance coupled with wide Interquartile Ranges (IQR), which points to massive sub-clonal heterogeneity.\n","* **Mechanism Over Origin:** Hierarchical Z-score clustering and macro pathway mapping demonstrated that a drug's target network (e.g., Mitosis, DNA Replication) serves as the primary driver of response architecture. Cellular destruction profiles across solid tumors are governed more by shared, target-specific pathway interactions than by the anatomical site where the tumor originated.\n","* **The Multi-Omic Switchboard:** Due to extreme structural class imbalances within binary mutation categories, formal parametric hypothesis testing was rejected to safeguard against statistical errors. However, effect-size bubble mapping revealed that permanent structural copy number modifications (`CNA`) and broad epigenetic silencing (`METHYLATION`) exert more stable, long-term shifts on global sensitivity shapes than transient transcriptomic variations (`GENE_EXPR`).\n","\n","---\n","\n","### 🚀 Limitations & Roadmap for Future Studies\n","1. **Resolving Minority Sample Scarcity:** To fully explore the hidden drivers within multi-omic features, future versions of this pipeline will incorporate synthetic oversampling algorithms (such as SMOTE) or specialized zero-shot pharmacogenomic architectures. This will help generate robust statistical power despite the natural scarcity of modified (\"Y\") mutation entries.\n","2. **Dynamic Synergy Modeling:** This analysis tracked therapeutic responses on an individual compound basis. The next phase will expand the pipeline to evaluate drug-drug combination matrices, modeling synergistic scoring indices to uncover mechanisms for overcoming solid tumor resistance lines.\n","3. **Translational Machine Learning:** Leveraging the multi-dimensional screening matrices generated in this project, future milestones include training predictive deep learning networks (such as Graph Neural Networks or Random Forest Regressors) to map patient-specific multi-omic profiles directly to therapeutic response indices.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"cqCaBzwEzVHT"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":[],"metadata":{"id":"tTtZlRz8zW5t"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]}],"metadata":{"accelerator":"GPU","colab":{"gpuType":"T4","provenance":[{"file_id":"1Ai6Q8ISUnV1B-VpX6iO-8dOgm77h-rit","timestamp":1789210685485},{"file_id":"1r8VYUHtp9tiGmqoGrt_ufb1rwWhkkbfr","timestamp":1778577927562}]},"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python"}},"nbformat":4,"nbformat_minor":0}